40,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some interesting stuff! Transport costs vary wildly depending on how far we go—it can be a huge chunk of the budget. But the public beds are surprisingly cheap and simple!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is good to know the public beds are affordable, Mio. However, I am concerned that some members have missed past camps entirely. We must choose a place that encourages everyone to attend and truly connect.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The public beds might be cheap, but the booking process is a nightmare. It's a lottery with a nine-page application that requires a full resubmission for any date change. That is an unacceptable administrative burden for the organizers.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if the public beds are that hard to book, maybe we should look at other options! But I found out that some inland places cram eight people into one room. That sounds way too crowded for a good sleep!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The club hall is not a viable option; the schedule is too crowded, and we'd be forced into inconvenient hours. Also, a third of our members can't arrive early without overnight costs, which we must factor into the budget.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, a nine-page application sounds like a total nightmare! But if the beds are that cheap, maybe the savings are worth the effort? Or maybe we can find a middle ground that isn't so stressful to book.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, while saving money is helpful, we must not forget the heart of the camp. If the environment is too rigid or stressful, it may discourage our members from joining us. We need a place that feels welcoming.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the savings are not worth the cost of burnout. Last year, the organizers lost significant personal time to duties. Adding a tedious lottery process on top of that is unreasonable. We need a streamlined booking system.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji I totally agree! No one should be stressed out before the camp even starts. But we can't just pick any place; if we're all squeezed together like sardines, we'll be grumpy and tired! We need space to actually sleep!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, we cannot prioritize ""cheap"" if the costs are unpredictable. If a third of the members need overnight stays just to arrive on time, those hidden expenses will quickly erase any savings from public beds.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that's a really good point about the hidden costs. If some people are spending more just to get there, the flat fee might not be fair. We need a spot that's accessible for everyone!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, exactly. If the travel is too difficult or the atmosphere too cold, we risk losing more members. I believe a place where we all stay together will help the different year-groups finally bond.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, bonding is important, but not at the expense of the organizers' sanity. I also found that self-catering cost the duty pair two hours daily last year. We must prioritize facilities with provided meals to reduce on-site labor.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, meals are a great idea! But listen, I found out that renting a whole building can be risky because if someone cancels, we all have to pay more. We need a place that's cozy but not too crowded!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, that is exactly the kind of financial risk we must avoid. A whole-building let with a variable cost per person is too unstable. We need a fixed, guaranteed price to ensure the club account isn't drained again.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Rin, @Misaki, you're right! If a cancellation makes everyone pay more, that's not fair at all. We need a place that's affordable, easy to book, and doesn't leave anyone paying extra just to join in!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we are all searching for a delicate balance. Let us look for a place that is easy to manage and fair in cost, yet warm enough to bring our lonely hearts together.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"To summarize, we must avoid any option that involves a lottery system, complex paperwork, or self-catering. The organizers' time is a finite resource; we cannot afford to waste it on bureaucracy or kitchen duty.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Rin,,"And we can't have a place where we're all squeezed in! If we don't get enough sleep, we'll be too tired to have any fun. Let's pick somewhere comfortable and easy for everyone!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We must prioritize financial stability. Any option with variable pricing or hidden travel costs is a risk we cannot take. I will only support a destination with a fixed, transparent cost that protects the club's remaining funds.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
