64,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at the options, Option A seems the safest for the budget, but Option C sounds like so much fun! However, @Misaki and @Rin, we have to be careful about those hidden costs and cancellation risks.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, you are right to be cautious. However, Option A may feel too much like a school day. For our members to truly bond and forget their year-groups, we need a change of scenery.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is out of the question. It uses the municipal system, which means the lottery and that nine-page application. I will not support an option that imposes such a heavy administrative burden on the organizers.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I agree with @Ryuji! Option B sounds like a nightmare. Plus, those inland centers cram too many people in one room. We'll be exhausted! I think Option C is the best for sleeping and having fun!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option C is too risky. A whole-building let with a new provider often leads to unpredictable costs. Option A is the only choice that allows us to control the budget precisely and avoid financial gaps.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I get that A is safe, but if we have to pay separately for those who live far away, isn't that just another uneven cost? I'm worried some people will end up paying way more than others!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, you have a kind heart to worry about that. If we choose Option A, the members who stay separately will be isolated from the rest of us during the evenings, which is exactly when the bonding happens.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, @Mio, you're right about the social aspect, but Option C is the most logical. It provides meals, eliminating the cooking duty that burned out last year's organizers. It's a far better balance of labor and experience than A or B.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, exactly! And @Misaki, if we get our own building at the lodge, we won't be squeezed eight to a room like at the inland centers. We'll actually get some sleep and have energy for training!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, @Rin, convenience and sleep are secondary to solvency. Option C's ""meals arranged through the owner"" is a red flag for variable pricing. I cannot risk another deficit. Option A's separate costs are transparent and manageable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, but if we go with A, we're still dealing with different costs for different people! Option C is exciting, but if the price changes last minute, it's not fair. Is there any way to fix the price for C?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, perhaps we can ask the owner for a fixed package. If we can secure that, Option C would be a wonderful way to ensure no one is left out and everyone can bond.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, that is a reasonable suggestion. If we can secure a fixed price, Option C solves both the financial instability and the labor issue. It is the only option that protects the organizers from burnout and bureaucracy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Misaki, please! If we pick A, it's just like being in class. We need a real trip! Option C is the only one where we can actually relax and sleep well without being crowded!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, @Shizue, a ""reasonable suggestion"" is not a guarantee. Without a signed contract, we are guessing. I cannot gamble the club's funds on a hope. Option A is the only choice that ensures we don't go into debt.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, I really want to be fair to everyone's wallet, but A feels too lonely for some. Since @Ryuji and @Rin are so against B and A, I'll vote for Option C! Let's just be super careful with the budget!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Ryuji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Mio. While Misaki's caution is wise, we cannot ignore the risk of members drifting away. Option C offers the warmth and togetherness we need to heal our divisions. I shall vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will vote for Option C. It is the only choice that eliminates the crushing administrative burden of Option B and the labor-intensive cooking duties of Option A. We must protect the organizers from burnout.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm voting for Option C too! We can't do B because of the crowds and the paperwork, and A is just boring. Let's go to the coast and actually get some sleep! Option C it is!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot support a gamble. Option C's lack of a fixed price is a liability we cannot afford. To protect the club's remaining funds and ensure total transparency, I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
